.TH VC4INFER 1 "2026-11-20" "vc4infer 1.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vc4infer \- run fixed-shape fp32 ONNX graphs on the VideoCore IV QPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc4infer
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vc4infer
executes a fixed-shape, batch-1, fp32 ONNX graph on the VideoCore IV (V3D)
QPUs of a Raspberry Pi 1/2/3, Zero or CM1/CM3.
Every float operation (convolutions, GEMMs, elementwise, pooling, softmax) is
dispatched to
.BR libvc4infer ;
the ARM cores only move bytes, pad, gather, concatenate and perform integer
shape bookkeeping.
An operator, attribute or shape the engine cannot dispatch raises
.B UnsupportedNode
naming the node and its ONNX op type.
There is no CPU arithmetic fallback.
.PP
Unprivileged runs go through the
.B vc4d
helper daemon on
.IR /run/vc4d.sock ,
which owns
.I /dev/mem
and the V3D register window.
The client opens neither.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fImodel.onnx\fR \-\-input \fIimage|csv|npy\fR [\-\-imgsz N] [\-\-conf 0.25] [\-\-iou 0.45] [\-\-json]
Run one inference.
Images (JPEG/PNG/BMP/WebP) are letterboxed to the model input size, converted
to RGB/fp32 and normalised to [0,1].
A YOLOv8/YOLO11 detection head is decoded on the host (boxes from the
cx,cy,w,h rows, best class, confidence threshold, class-aware NMS) and the
boxes are mapped back to the original image pixels.
An annotated image is written next to the input unless
.B \-\-no\-save
is given.
With
.B \-\-json
the command prints a single JSON document: model, input, timings, decoded
detections and the annotated image path.
.TP
.B bench \fImodel.onnx\fR [\-\-imgsz N] [\-\-reps N]
Time the graph end to end.
One warm-up run performs the kernel JIT and is reported separately, then
.B \-\-reps
(default 3) timed runs.
Prints milliseconds per image (mean, median, best), FPS, launches per image,
GPU (pack + kernel) time as a fraction of wall time, and arena / graph-pool /
peak memory.
.TP
.B nodes \fImodel.onnx\fR [\-v]
Static coverage report: node counts per ONNX op, a supported/unsupported
verdict for every node, the names and reasons for the unsupported ones, and the
number of
.B Mul(x, Sigmoid(x))
pairs that fuse into a single SiLU launch.
The executor stays authoritative:
.B nodes
reads the graph, attributes and initialiser shapes; it does not run it.
.TP
.B selftest
Run the shipped reference models (modelA, modelB, modelC and the real YOLOv8n
COCO export at 160x160) against their stored CPU references with
atol = rtol = 5e-4.
Exits 0 when every element of every output is inside tolerance, 1 otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, the resolved engine library, the onnx/numpy versions, the
backend and the kernel-cache path.
.TP
.BI \-\-conf " x"
Confidence threshold for detections (default 0.25).
.TP
.BI \-\-iou " x"
NMS IoU threshold (default 0.45).
.TP
.BI \-\-imgsz " N"
Letterbox size.
It must match the model's static input size; the model cannot be resized at
run time.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " dir"
Kernel blob cache.
Default
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/vc4infer/kcache
(or
.IR ~/.cache/vc4infer/kcache ).
The first run JIT-compiles the kernels for the graph (about a second) and
stores them there.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VC4INFER_DAEMON
1 (the default set by the CLI) uses vc4d; 0 uses the direct
.I /dev/mem
backend and needs root.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_ARENA_MB
Arena size to request from vc4d (default 64, daemon-capped).
.TP
.B VC4_POOL_RESERVE_MB
Bytes kept free for per-convolution scratch (default 24; use 40 for 320x320).
.TP
.B VC4INFER_CACHE
Kernel blob cache directory.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_KGEN
Alternative
.I kgen.py
kernel generator (default
.IR /usr/lib/vc4infer/kgen/kgen.py ).
.TP
.B VC4_NO_SILU_FUSE
1 disables the
.B Mul(x, Sigmoid(x)) -> Silu
graph rewrite (A/B measurement only; about 15% slower).
.SH SUPPORTED NODES
Conv (1x1/3x3, stride 1/2, group 1 or depthwise), Relu, Sigmoid, Silu, Add,
Mul, Sub, Div (by a constant), MaxPool, Concat, Split, Slice, Resize (nearest),
Transpose, Softmax (<= 16 classes), MatMul, Gemm, GlobalAveragePool, Reshape,
Flatten, Squeeze, Unsqueeze, Cast, Identity, Constant, Shape, Gather.
Batch 1 and fp32 only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libvc4infer.so.1
The engine.
.TP
.I /usr/include/vc4infer.h
The C API.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/vc4infer.py
The ctypes binding.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/vc4infer/kgen/
The QPU kernel generator used to JIT blobs.
.TP
.I /usr/share/vc4infer/models/
The selftest models and their stored inputs and references.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
vc4infer nodes yolov8n.onnx
vc4infer run yolov8n.onnx --input bus.jpg --imgsz 160
vc4infer run yolov8n.onnx --input bus.jpg --imgsz 160 --json
vc4infer bench yolov8n.onnx --reps 5
vc4infer selftest
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
1 when selftest reports a mismatch.
2 on a usage error.
3 when the model needs an unsupported node or shape.
.SH PYTHON API
The same engine is importable:
.B import vc4infer
provides
.B Engine
(raw numpy outputs, plan, profile, memory),
.B Device
and a thin
.B yolo.Detector
on top of
.B postprocess.decode_yolo
and
.BR postprocess.nms .
The wheel is pure Python and uses the engine library installed by this package:
.RS
.nf
pip install https://rughinnit.github.io/vc4top/pip/vc4infer-1.1.2-py3-none-any.whl
.fi
.RE
See
.I /usr/share/doc/vc4infer/PYTHON-API.md
and the examples in
.IR /usr/share/doc/vc4infer/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vc4top (1)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/vc4infer/README.md
for measured performance, the supported-node table, the 320x320 arena recipe
and the known limits.
